{#
  T-3.08 — the footer.

  EVERY LINK COMES FROM THE STORE MENU, AND THAT IS WHAT CLOSES OP-2. The
  register recorded an open question: the artboard's «روابط مهمة» column lists
  «المدونة» as a destination, but the blog was ruled out as the Stories source on
  2026-08-06, and three readings were possible. Building the column from
  `salla-menu source="footer"` **makes the question moot rather than answering
  it** — whether «المدونة» appears is the merchant's own footer menu in the Salla
  dashboard, and the theme neither adds the link nor removes it. Nothing here
  references `blog_link`, which was reading 2's requirement, and the link renders
  when the merchant wants it, which was reading 1's. See /docs/DERIVED-DECISIONS.md.

  WHAT THE DESIGN OMITS AND THIS TEMPLATE DROPS: upstream's `salla-apps-icons`
  and `salla-contacts` blocks. The artboard draws neither, and unlike the badges
  on a product card, the data behind them has other homes — the WhatsApp FAB in
  T-3.10 and Salla's own contact page. The design wins where the information is
  not orphaned.

  WHAT THE DESIGN OMITS AND THIS TEMPLATE KEEPS: the VAT number and the copyright
  hook. A tax disclosure has **no other home in this theme**, and the copyright
  line is injected by the platform through a hook rather than authored here.
  Dropping either to match an artboard would be tidiness at the expense of a
  legal obligation.
#}
<footer data-testid="store-footer" class="store-footer">
    {# T-2.18 — the footer is a panel like every other section: the container
       carries the 16px page gutter and the panel fills its content box. #}
    <div class="container">
    <div class="store-footer__inner s-block__panel">
        <a href="{{ link('/') }}" class="store-footer__brand">
            <img src="{{ store.logo|cdn(175) }}" alt="{{ store.name }}" width="175" height="40" loading="lazy">
        </a>

        <nav class="store-footer__links" aria-labelledby="footer-links-heading">
            <h2 class="store-footer__heading" id="footer-links-heading">{{ trans('blocks.footer.pages_links') }}</h2>
            <salla-menu data-testid="store-footer-menu" source="footer" with-cookie-preferences></salla-menu>
        </nav>

        <hr class="store-footer__rule">

        {# `salla-social` labels its own links and reflects only the networks the
           merchant configured — so the row is six pills or two, without the theme
           deciding which. Styled from outside; the component is not replaced. #}
        <salla-social data-testid="store-footer-social" class="store-footer__social"></salla-social>

        {# T-3.09 — CORRECTING T-3.08's COMMENT, WHICH NAMED THE WRONG BADGE.
           `salla-trust-badges` carries **no Maroof**: it renders the commercial
           register number, or the freelance document number when there is no
           commercial one, and nothing else. Read from the component's own source.
           It is kept because for a `store_country` of `SA` the component forces
           its own visibility as a legal requirement — hiding it is not the
           theme's call to make — and because the artboard draws no register
           number, so nothing here contradicts a design that is silent. #}
        <salla-trust-badges data-testid="store-footer-trust-badges"
                            class="store-footer__badges"
                            {% if theme.settings.get('footer_is_dark') %}dark{% endif %}></salla-trust-badges>

        {#
          T-3.09 — the marks, all of them from the platform. B9: the theme ships
          no third-party mark as a bundled image, and `src/assets/images/` holds
          none. `salla-payments` renders `store.settings.payments` — the methods
          the merchant actually enabled — from Salla's CDN, so the row is six
          marks or two without this theme deciding which.

          THE BADGE THE ARTBOARD DRAWS IS NOT MAROOF. The backlog calls it a
          Maroof badge; the export draws the **Saudi Business Center** mark with
          «موثق في منصة الأعمال» beside it. Maroof exists nowhere in the SDK — it
          is a `store.social` key, not a badge — and SBC is a different registry.
          `salla-payments` already renders this badge, already gates it on
          `store.settings.certificate.id`, and already wraps it in an
          `<a target="_blank">` to `eauthenticate.saudibusiness.gov.sa`, **which
          is the acceptance criterion's "real registration"**. So the link is the
          platform's and is not re-implemented here.

          What the slots are for. The component's default SBC item is a bare
          image with `alt="SBC"` and no label; the artboard gives it the caption
          above. The default payment item carries `width="100%" height="100%"`,
          which are not valid `<img>` dimensions, so the browser reserves nothing
          — the marks come from the CDN at 58×58 and are declared as such here.
          `{image}`, `{link}` and `{payment}` are the component's own
          placeholders. `<template>` rather than a live element, so an
          un-substituted `{image}` can never paint.

          ⚠ THE `<li>` OPENS ON THE SAME LINE AS THE `<template>`, ON PURPOSE.
          The component finishes by running `el.replaceWith(el.firstChild)` over
          the wrapper it rendered the slot into — `firstChild`, not
          `firstElementChild`. A newline after `<template …>` makes the first
          child a **whitespace text node**, so the wrapper would be replaced by
          that text and the mark itself silently dropped. Upstream's defaults are
          single-line strings and never meet this. Do not reformat.
        #}
        {# `role="group"` and not a bare `aria-label`: the host is a custom element
           with no implicit role, and a label on a roleless element is not reliably
           exposed. The role is what makes the name reach assistive tech. #}
        <salla-payments data-testid="store-footer-payments"
                        class="store-footer__payments"
                        role="group"
                        aria-label="{{ trans('theme.footer.payments_label') }}">
            <template slot="sbc"><li class="s-payments-list-item store-footer__sbc">
                <a href="{link}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    {# The caption names the link, so the mark itself is decorative
                       — alt="" keeps it from being announced twice. #}
                    <img src="{image}" alt="" width="58" height="58" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
                    <span>{{ trans('theme.footer.sbc_verified') }}</span>
                </a>
            </li></template>

            {# `{payment}` is the method's slug, which is the only per-mark
               identity the platform exposes. A slug→name map would be a
               hard-coded list that goes stale the day Salla adds a method. #}
            <template slot="payment"><li class="s-payments-list-item">
                <img src="{image}" alt="{payment}" width="58" height="58" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
            </li></template>

            {# Cash on delivery carries the same invalid `width="100%"` in its
               default item, and it is a payment method like any other. #}
            <template slot="cod"><li class="s-payments-list-item">
                <img src="{image}" alt="{{ trans('theme.footer.cod') }}" width="58" height="58" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
            </li></template>
        </salla-payments>

        {% if store.settings.tax.number %}
            <div class="store-footer__tax">
                <span>{{ trans('common.elements.tax_number') }}</span>
                <b class="bidi-ltr">{{ store.settings.tax.number }}</b>

                {% if store.settings.tax.certificate %}
                    <a class="load-img-onclick" data-modal-id="modal-value-tax" href="#/">
                        <img width="40" height="50" src="{{ 'images/tax.png'|cdn(70,70) }}" loading="lazy"
                             alt="{{ trans('common.elements.tax_number') }}">
                    </a>
                {% endif %}
            </div>

            {% if store.settings.tax.certificate %}
                <salla-modal data-testid="store-footer-tax-modal"
                             sub-title-first
                             sub-title="{{ trans('common.elements.tax_number') }}"
                             modal-title="{{ store.settings.tax.number }}"
                             id="modal-value-tax">
                    <div class="flex justify-center max-w-full">
                        <img class="w-full" loading="lazy"
                             data-src="{{ store.settings.tax.certificate }}"
                             alt="{{ store.settings.tax.number }}">
                    </div>
                </salla-modal>
            {% endif %}
        {% endif %}

        <p class="store-footer__copyright copyright-text">{% hook copyright %}</p>
    </div>
    </div>
</footer>
